cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QuantumNovelty in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "QuantumNovelty: an audit-and-falsify framework for quantum-computing research papers"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kashani"
    given-names: "Shlomo"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-06-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/BoltzmannEntropy/QuantumNovelty"
url: "https://boltzmannentropy.github.io/QuantumNovelty.github.io/"
abstract: >-
  Agent-skill framework for writing and reviewing quantum-computing
  papers: a 5-voice referee panel with a deterministic quality gate, an
  11-fallacy quantum-CS taxonomy, strict-domination novelty audits, and
  an exact token + USD cost ledger on every LLM call. Runs on the Claude
  Code CLI by default.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - peer review
  - LLM agents
  - research automation
  - novelty audit
